1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:02,490
Assalamualaikum, Farhan.

2
00:00:03,380 --> 00:00:07,253
Thank you, Farhan, for having your time
here.

3
00:00:07,253 --> 00:00:09,943
I know you have been through a very
difficult time.

4
00:00:11,193 --> 00:00:13,143
So, how are you feeling today?

5
00:00:15,333 --> 00:00:17,623
I'm okay. Just a minute.

6
00:00:17,773 --> 00:00:20,943
Just a minute. I can stop thinking about
that case.

7
00:00:21,553 --> 00:00:23,733
Never mind, Farhan.

8
00:00:23,733 --> 00:00:28,263
Take your time. We can sit quietly here to
discuss.

9
00:00:28,333 --> 00:00:32,523
Or maybe you don't have to do this thing
to me until you are ready.

10
00:00:33,727 --> 00:00:35,307
Honestly, not that great.

11
00:00:35,307 --> 00:00:40,297
I know these things happen, but I keep
replaying every step in my head.

12
00:00:40,507 --> 00:00:43,837
It sounds like the event is still in your
mind.

13
00:00:44,167 --> 00:00:46,317
Even the procedure has ended.

14
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:50,610
Yes, the patient wasn't expected to die.

15
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:53,240
Everything happened so quickly.

16
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:54,490
We tried everything.

17
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:58,970
The whole team was resuscitating, but we
couldn't save the patient.

18
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:07,790
That must be incredibly difficult for you,
since your work is to save someone's life.

19
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:10,840
I keep wondering whether I missed
something.

20
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:14,350
Maybe I should have recognised the
deterioration earlier.

21
00:01:14,883 --> 00:01:20,233
I hear how much responsibility that you
have to bear.

22
00:01:21,843 --> 00:01:28,263
I know I want you to know that this is a
space to discuss or to open up, because we

23
00:01:28,263 --> 00:01:29,733
are not here to judge you.

24
00:01:30,023 --> 00:01:33,193
So, I'm here to listen and support you.

25
00:01:34,690 --> 00:01:39,570
I know we all did what we could, but I
still feel like I should have seen it

26
00:01:39,570 --> 00:01:40,570
coming.

27
00:01:42,053 --> 00:01:46,673
I know it is understandable that the
moments keep replaying in your heart and

28
00:01:46,673 --> 00:01:47,673
in your mind.

29
00:01:49,313 --> 00:01:52,633
Sometimes we are always questioning our
decision.

30
00:01:52,633 --> 00:01:53,573
Whether it's a decision or not.

31
00:01:53,573 --> 00:01:54,903
Whether it's right or wrong.

32
00:01:57,033 --> 00:02:01,127
I keep hearing the monitor in my head
every day, every night.

33
00:02:01,517 --> 00:02:07,507
Even when I close my eyes, I still can
hear the monitor.

34
00:02:07,717 --> 00:02:11,997
That sounds exhausting Farhan, since you
are already away from the operation

35
00:02:11,997 --> 00:02:12,997
theatre.

36
00:02:15,637 --> 00:02:20,797
Yes. I haven't been sleeping properly for
almost a few days.

37
00:02:20,797 --> 00:02:23,797
I haven't been eaten properly since it
happened.

38
00:02:23,797 --> 00:02:25,467
No quality of life.

39
00:02:26,340 --> 00:02:31,660
Um... Well, thank you for telling me that
you have this...

40
00:02:31,660 --> 00:02:35,710
I understand this affects you emotionally
and physically.

41
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:43,100
And I want you to understand something
that feeling distressed after a patient

42
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:48,510
died unexpectedly does not mean that you
are weak or you are not competent.

43
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:54,050
Everyone seems to be.

44
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:55,690
I've moved on.

45
00:02:56,140 --> 00:03:00,090
I feel like I am the only one struggling
right now.

46
00:03:00,713 --> 00:03:07,793
Well, sometimes when people respond
differently to different situations, it

47
00:03:07,793 --> 00:03:11,623
doesn't mean that they appear okay.

48
00:03:11,993 --> 00:03:13,653
They are not affected.

49
00:03:13,653 --> 00:03:17,763
You don't have to compare your reaction
with others.

50
00:03:19,293 --> 00:03:21,723
You know what? I feel very guilty.

51
00:03:21,813 --> 00:03:23,933
Maybe I should be stronger than this.

52
00:03:23,933 --> 00:03:29,453
You are human before you become an
anesthesiologist.

53
00:03:31,363 --> 00:03:39,033
It's okay for you to feel sad or shaken,
confused or even feel guilty.

54
00:03:40,303 --> 00:03:43,913
You don't have to force yourself to be
strong all the time.

55
00:03:44,303 --> 00:03:50,053
To be honest, I don't really want to go
back to the theatre right now.

56
00:03:50,243 --> 00:03:52,473
I almost call in sick tomorrow.

57
00:03:52,823 --> 00:03:58,093
I don't know. I don't know if I can trust
even myself anymore.

58
00:03:59,583 --> 00:04:01,713
I appreciate your honesty, Farhan.

59
00:04:02,503 --> 00:04:06,853
It sounds that you are overwhelmed and not
ready to go to work.

60
00:04:07,483 --> 00:04:14,663
Yeah, I am worried that if something
happens again, I may not be able to cope

61
00:04:14,663 --> 00:04:16,213
with the situation anymore.

62
00:04:17,363 --> 00:04:22,163
Given your experience, I know that you
deserve attention.

63
00:04:22,163 --> 00:04:26,413
Can I ask why you don't trust yourself?

64
00:04:27,283 --> 00:04:33,213
Are you worried about your ability to
perform in the future?

65
00:04:33,943 --> 00:04:38,813
I mean, I'm afraid that I won't be able to
focus properly.

66
00:04:39,003 --> 00:04:40,883
I just feel mentally exhausted.

67
00:04:40,883 --> 00:04:42,513
I just want to rest.

68
00:04:43,173 --> 00:04:45,833
Well, thank you for clarifying.

69
00:04:45,833 --> 00:04:48,423
Your well-being and safety matters.

70
00:04:48,653 --> 00:04:51,933
So, I would encourage for you to discuss.

71
00:04:51,933 --> 00:04:53,703
With your immediate support.

72
00:04:53,893 --> 00:04:59,583
Maybe to render whether you are ready or
not to return to duties.

73
00:05:00,940 --> 00:05:06,250
But I am afraid people will think that I
am not capable of doing my job.

74
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:08,730
Don't worry. Don't worry.

75
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:14,610
Seeking support is not a sign of
incompetence.

76
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:19,270
You are actually recognizing a symptom.

77
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:23,660
This is important. Because you know you
need help.

78
00:05:23,660 --> 00:05:28,610
You need help. And you want to be ready
before you go to work.

79
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:31,330
So, what should I do now?

80
00:05:32,047 --> 00:05:34,737
Well, can we start from the basics?

81
00:05:36,507 --> 00:05:38,527
Have you had enough rest?

82
00:05:38,527 --> 00:05:39,867
Have you been eating?

83
00:05:39,867 --> 00:05:42,177
Is there someone that you can rely on?

84
00:05:42,607 --> 00:05:43,657
Not really.

85
00:05:44,327 --> 00:05:47,277
I've just been keeping everything to
myself.

86
00:05:47,993 --> 00:05:51,443
Okay. You don't have to manage this alone.

87
00:05:51,493 --> 00:05:53,793
We can explore practical support.

88
00:05:53,793 --> 00:05:55,863
Maybe we can find for you.

89
00:05:57,013 --> 00:06:03,123
Your supervisor can supervise your current
capacity of your clinical judgment.

90
00:06:03,373 --> 00:06:07,483
You need time. We understand you need time
to recover.

91
00:06:07,673 --> 00:06:11,523
And we will arrange follow-up for you
later.

92
00:06:12,220 --> 00:06:15,790
I think I need that support.

93
00:06:16,760 --> 00:06:19,780
Good. Good. That's a good first step.

94
00:06:21,010 --> 00:06:23,980
Let's not pressure to answer everything
today.

95
00:06:24,550 --> 00:06:26,940
We can go this step by step.

96
00:06:28,430 --> 00:06:32,160
I don't know. I still don't know how to
stop thinking about that patient.

97
00:06:34,570 --> 00:06:40,610
I don't force you to quickly switch off
the thoughts.

98
00:06:40,610 --> 00:06:46,620
So, when they come, we try not to
recognize them without judging yourself.

99
00:06:47,470 --> 00:06:48,910
You have to give permission.

100
00:06:48,910 --> 00:06:54,710
You have to give time for yourself to
regulate, to eat regularly, to go and

101
00:06:54,710 --> 00:07:02,340
rest. And we want you to reconnect back to
your friends and colleagues.

102
00:07:02,350 --> 00:07:07,760
We also can work together on strategies to
manage any distressing moments.

103
00:07:08,660 --> 00:07:13,170
I suppose I never thought that doctors
could be affected this much by losing a

104
00:07:13,170 --> 00:07:14,333
patient.

105
00:07:14,333 --> 00:07:19,280
Well, you have to understand healthcare
professionals are also often affected

106
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:22,279
during the care for your patients.

107
00:07:22,279 --> 00:07:26,160
Sometimes we forget that we also need
care.

108
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:32,230
You deserve the same compassion as much as
how much you give to your patients.

109
00:07:34,567 --> 00:07:42,667
Thank you. I didn't realize how much I
needed someone just to sit and listen

110
00:07:42,667 --> 00:07:43,667
to me.

111
00:07:44,413 --> 00:07:49,023
I'm glad you shared with me today, Farhan.

112
00:07:50,073 --> 00:07:52,013
Remember, you are not alone.

113
00:07:52,013 --> 00:07:53,563
We will work this together,

114
00:07:55,033 --> 00:07:57,863
right, at a pace that manageable for you.

115
00:07:58,473 --> 00:08:00,963
Thank you. I feel a little bit lighter.

116
00:08:02,153 --> 00:08:03,883
Before we finish,

117
00:08:04,193 --> 00:08:07,523
maybe we can arrange more session after
this?

118
00:08:07,913 --> 00:08:09,503
Thank you so much. I really need that
support.

119
00:08:10,033 --> 00:08:12,133
Okay, thank you.

120
00:08:12,133 --> 00:08:13,183
Thank you.

